ven-names></name><name><surname>Lasmezas</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dormont</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neurotoxicity of the putative transmembrane domain of the prion protein</article-title><source>Neurobiol Dis</source><year>2000</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>644</fpage><lpage>656</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11114262</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/nbdi.2000.0316</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A transmembrane form of the prion protein is localized in the golgi apparatus of neurons</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2005</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>15855</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671025</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.M412298200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiesa</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prion diseases: what is the neurotoxic molecule?</article-title><source>Neurobiol Dis</source><year>2001</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>743</fpage><lpage>763</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11592845</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1006/nbdi.2001.0433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hegde</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rane</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prion protein trafficking and the development of neurodegeneration</article-title><source>Trends Neurosci</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>339</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12850426</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0166-2236(03)00143-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nichols</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>GM1-containing lipid rafts are depleted within clathrin-coated pits</article-title><source>Curr Biol</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>686</fpage><lpage>690</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12699627</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00209-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sugimoto</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Ninomiya</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohsaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Higaki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Davies</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ioannou</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohno</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Accumulation of cholera toxin and GM1 ganglioside in the early endosome of Niemann-Pick C1-deficient cells</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>12391</fpage><lpage>12396</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11675488</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.221181998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>PU</given-names></name><name><surname>Nabi</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distinct caveolae-mediated endocytic pathways target the Golgi apparatus and the endoplasmic reticulum</article-title><source>J Cell Sci</source><year>2003</y